Campfire wasm patch 0103: connect only to the configured node.

NodeNetwork::tryToConnect added BEAM's built-in peers (default_peers.cpp:
eu-nodes / us-nodes.mainnet.beam.mw:8100) to the user's node on every connect
and reconnect, and fell back to peers advertised by nodes when the configured
name did not resolve. In the browser that dialled servers the user never chose
(wss://...:8100, measured: 18 attempts in 80 s), each of which would learn the
user's IP address. With a node configured, it is now the only node; the
defaults and the advertised fallbacks are used only when no node is given.
Applied to the wasm tree only (the desktop/Android cores are unchanged).

--- a/wallet/core/node_network.cpp
+++ b/wallet/core/node_network.cpp
@@ -44,8 +44,15 @@
         }
 
         m_timer->start(RECONNECTION_TIMEOUT, false, [this]() {
-            auto nodeAddresses = getDefaultPeers();
-            nodeAddresses.push_back(m_nodeAddress);
+            // Campfire: a configured node is the only node. Adding BEAM's
+            // built-in peers (default_peers.cpp) made the browser dial
+            // eu-nodes/us-nodes:8100 on every (re)connect, handing the user's IP
+            // address to servers they never chose. Defaults only without a node.
+            std::vector<std::string> nodeAddresses;
+            if (m_nodeAddress.empty())
+                nodeAddresses = getDefaultPeers();
+            else
+                nodeAddresses.push_back(m_nodeAddress);
             for (const auto& addr : nodeAddresses)
             {
                 io::Address nodeAddr;
@@ -67,7 +74,9 @@
             }
 
             BEAM_LOG_WARNING() << "User-specified nodes cannot be resolved.";
-            if (!m_fallbackAddresses.empty())
